From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/display: keep the CRTC's color transforms

The display WSI clears GAMMA_LUT, DEGAMMA_LUT and CTM on the CRTC when it
first takes the display, so that a transform left behind by another user
does not colour a Vulkan application. On PortareOS those properties are
the panel's calibration - a measured correction the launcher sets once
for everything scanned out - and clearing them undid it for every game
started through RetroArch's Vulkan driver. Leave them as found.

Signed-off-by: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
---
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_display.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_display.c
@@ -2930,15 +2930,12 @@
       drmModeAtomicAddProperty(req, crtc_id, connector->crtc_property[MODE_ID], blob_id);
       drmModeAtomicAddProperty(req, crtc_id, connector->crtc_property[ACTIVE], 1);
 
-      /* Disable any color transforms that may have been previously set on the
-       * CRTC by another user.
+      /* PortareOS: the CRTC's color transforms - DEGAMMA_LUT, CTM,
+       * GAMMA_LUT - are the panel's calibration, set once by the launcher
+       * for everything that is ever scanned out. Upstream clears them here
+       * on the grounds that another user may have left them behind; on this
+       * device that other user is the one who meant them. Leave them be.
        */
-      if (connector->crtc_property[GAMMA_LUT] != -1)
-         drmModeAtomicAddProperty(req, crtc_id, connector->crtc_property[GAMMA_LUT], 0);
-      if (connector->crtc_property[DEGAMMA_LUT] != -1)
-         drmModeAtomicAddProperty(req, crtc_id, connector->crtc_property[DEGAMMA_LUT], 0);
-      if (connector->crtc_property[CTM] != -1)
-         drmModeAtomicAddProperty(req, crtc_id, connector->crtc_property[CTM], 0);
 
       flags |= DRM_MODE_ATOMIC_ALLOW_MODESET;
    }
